+The kernel's Lean thread stack defaults to 64 MiB. Set `LEAN_STACK_SIZE_KB`
+to a positive size in KiB to override it, for example
+`LEAN_STACK_SIZE_KB=131072 bend PROOF.bend --verdict` for 128 MiB. Unset or
+empty uses the default. Deep proofs may need more; a stack too large for the
+host can prevent thread creation. This setting also reaches a `$BENDTT`
+executable; it does not change the proof or the kernel's checks.
